{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see","id":775260,"title":"Lunar Charms we want to see!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-26T22:19:45-08:00","id":775260,"title":"Lunar Charms we want to see!","content":"<b>Sleeping Dragon Awakens</b> was a very flavorful and powerful Charm from 2.5 that didn't get long to shine. But I have recently realized that the character of the Charm can be preserved by replacing the Overdrive mechanic with bonuses to your Join Battle roll. Rather than building up a stock of Offensive motes to blow away invaders to your territory, you can build up a stock of Initiative to seize the first strike and possibly end the battle with a single Decisive blow. Or at least take out one of the invaders before engaging the others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Who Disturbs My Slumber</b>, created by Reminiscent Oasis, can do the same. Instead of gaining offensive motes upon being rudely awoken from your sleep, you gain automatic successes to your Join Battle roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast Calming Method</b> would be a Charisma-based Charm that functions like Solar Friendship With Animals Approach, but without that Charm's Survival Ability limitations. With the Charm active, the Lunar doesn't register as a threat to anyone or anything -- wounded beasts, small prey animals, and mother hippos watching their young will allow him to approach and touch them, and territorial predators will allow him to pass through their hunting grounds unmolested so long as they are not hungry. The Lunar could even break into someone's home in full armor and bearing a bloody sword, and the homeowner will react with indignation regarding the trespass instead of fear for her life. Even the most convicted Immaculate, if she learned he was a Lunar Anathema, would believe that the silver demon meant her no harm. Those so affected will not mistake a lack of harmful intent for a lack of danger, however; Immaculate devotees will remember that devils are inherently corruptive, just as beasts that smell an infectious disease upon the Lunar would seek to flee or drive him away, and mice will take care that they are not trodden underfoot by accident.<br /> <br /> The effects of this Charm end immediately upon the Lunar deciding to engage in hostilities with any other present character, or otherwise take an action that would indirectly harm them. Studying someone with premeditated intent to harm them later with the information counts, though plotting murder against someone not present would not. The Charm cannot be reactivated for the rest of the scene, and will not work again on witnesses to the Lunar's hostility until the next day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dog-Tongue Method.</b> Speak any human language (or your own true voice!), so long as your current form is capable of vocalizing at all. Likewise, communicate with any animal species regardless of your form, so long as they communicate in a manner even vaguely possible with your form -- wearing the form of a wolf would be ineffective for conveying ideas to a species of octopus that exchange information primarily through changing color patterns. This Charm doesn't itself grant the Lunar knowledge of an animal species's language, nor incline animals to listen.<br /> <br /> <b>Stance-as-Thought Stride.</b> As the Solar Charm, Poetic Expression Style, but it additionally allows the Lunar to communicate simple ideas to animal species even without knowing their language. Having the appropriate Survival specialty allows the communication of complex ideas beyond what the animal's own language ought to convey, though the animal's own intelligence still limits the complexity of what they can understand.<br /> <br /> <b>Glance Oration Technique.</b> As Single-Voice Kata, but through body-language. The Lunar can speak, sing, or play an instrument in order to attract the attention of those who can hear but not immediately see him, but this Charm doesn't enable him to convey two different messages at once. Unlike Single Voice Kata, spirits and fair folk actually like this method of communication, but the Lunar's Appearance becomes capped by his Performance since these exotic beings are judging the delivery of his arguments based on the beauty of his interpretative dancing.<br /> <br /> <b>Secret Speech Method.</b> A Manipulation Charm that allows the Lunar to communicate one message to an individual or small group, and an entirely different message to everyone else. Explicitly compatible with Glance Oration Technique, allowing the Lunar to hide the message of his body language from the broader audience, or from a particular individual or subgroup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-27-2015, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T23:23:58-08:00","id":775288,"title":"","content":"Meerkat Steals the Spotlight, dunno what it would do, but I know someone has suggested it. If they see this maybe they can provide ideas for it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T23:29:47-08:00","id":775289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bulshock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=775288#post775288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meerkat Steals the Spotlight, dunno what it would do, but I know someone has suggested it. If they see this maybe they can provide ideas for it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe an upgrade to Attention Demanding Presence, which causes witnesses to forget most everything anyone else did in a scene because the Lunar was somehow more memorable.<br /> <br /> This allows a Lunar to help her party members out by taking the heat for them... and then hiding her identity by posing as someone or something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T23:31:40-08:00","id":775291,"title":"","content":"We all know that the best Lunar charm is and always will be Pumpkin Chariot Prana, but that's not applicable to EVERY game setting. Alas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T05:40:18-08:00","id":775411,"title":"","content":"Are you still wanting to do that one where the Lunar puts people in awe of her clever door-opening skills?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T08:11:59-08:00","id":775475,"title":"","content":"I always loved the territory charms and the elsewhere charms in 2e. I'm really looking forward to the return of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T08:31:03-08:00","id":775485,"title":"","content":"I just want Lunars to be able to do <a href=\"https://youtu.be/PEBevNq8Np4?t=1m6s\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Blade Snapping Cat Leap</b> as a disarm charm that also breaks a regular weapon. <b>Pride Guardian Dive </b>upgrade to reflexively use it against a foe that would strike an ally of the Lunar, once per scene bar resets.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 11-27-2015, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T09:37:54-08:00","id":775520,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see some charms that let the lunar make withering attacks by way of the disengage action and moving away from their foes, that encourage their foes to follow them to reduce damage, which allows multiple lunars the ability to split up large groups of foes. Like Wyld Hunts, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T09:43:17-08:00","id":775523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colin_Fredericks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=775475#post775475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always loved the territory charms and the elsewhere charms in 2e. I'm really looking forward to the return of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Elsewhere Den Charms, should they return at all, need to make a major change.<br /> <br /> I'd prefer them to be a set of &quot;sort of Craft&quot; Charms that give Lunars bonuses to constructing shelters. Not because the Lunar is skilled at crafting like a Solar, but because the Lunar is talented and inspired and impassioned about creating a safe haven.<br /> <br /> These Charms would include ways to make these shelters hidden and ways to make them larger on the inside than the outside. But there is no way to make them more difficult to enter than a spirit's sanctum, much less as impossible as the old Elsewhere Dens.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Lunar can't just retreat into Elsewhere wherever; her created refuge has a fixed point on the map. Between that and the inability to completely lock out the rest of the world, Lunars cannot simply remove themselves from Creation and its stories.<br /> <br /> (These Charms would also involve creating demesnes and manses.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T10:20:05-08:00","id":775534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=775411#post775411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you still wanting to do that one where the Lunar puts people in awe of her clever door-opening skills?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what you're talking about or who you're addressing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T10:55:33-08:00","id":775552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=775291#post775291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We all know that the best Lunar charm is and always will be Pumpkin Chariot Prana, but that's not applicable to EVERY game setting. Alas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pumpkin Chariot Prana is probably one of the easiest to take out of the Modern setting. Why yes, this ox cart does have the traits of a trireme.<br /> <br /> (albeit kind of a thematic cipher, so maybe not that great for Ex3 Lunars)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","user":"Robert Vance","date":". 11-27-2015, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T11:06:53-08:00","id":775557,"title":"","content":"&lt;stuff removed&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":643,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","user":"Taliesin","date":".  Not fitting the thread. 11-27-2015, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T11:07:09-08:00","id":775558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=775552#post775552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pumpkin Chariot Prana is probably one of the easiest to take out of the Modern setting. Why yes, this ox cart does have the traits of a trireme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably more of a Sidereal or Getimian trick, though.<br /> <br /> The much more Lunar trick is investing your totem into a vehicle to make it more figuratively and literally beastly.<br /> <br /> <br /> On which note, Charms I want for familiars:<ul><li>Automatically gain a familiar's Hearts Blood, just by having the familiar bond with the animal in question. The Heart's Blood is kept constantly fresh by the bond, you don't need to keep making &quot;back up&quot; save files every time you think your familiar might die soon.<ul><li>Treat a familiar's shape as one of your true forms, for as long as the familiar lives.</li> <li>Gain a second war form based on a familiar's shape, for as long the familiar lives.</li> <li>Gain a false Tell based on the familiar's shape, to mask your true Tell?</li> <li>Possibly one of multiple routes to Chimerahood?</li> </ul></li> <li>Gain Heart's Blood through a familiar's actions.</li> <li>Give a familiar human intelligence.<ul><li>Give familiar a war form and true human form of their own.</li> <li>Give familiar access to your True Forms.<ul><li>Give familiar access to your Heart's Blood library.</li> <li>Give familiar Lunar Charms?</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>See through familiar's eyes<ul><li>Act through the familiar, using your Abilities (and Attributes, where appropriate)<ul><li>Using your own or the familiar's Attributes as you please, with shapeshifting making anything appropriate.</li> <li>Exchange locations with your familiar by the two of you shapeshifting into each other, with necessary range and difficulty restrictions.</li> <li>Use your Charms through familiar.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Make your familiar a Chimera.</li> <li>Share health, Willpower and mote pools with your familiar and vice-versa</li> <li>Split off your Spirit Shape to act as a familiar, locking out your Spirit Shape and DBT for the duration; the subdivision is only as smart as a natural beast of that species would be, or only as smart as you could make a familar with the intelligence-increasing Charm. The death of this creature would be crippling if not fatal.</li> <li>Split off your birth form to act as a familiar, locking out your human form and DBT for the duration. Prerequires the ability to give a familiar human intelligence, with the subdivision of you being only as intelligent as the &quot;familiar intelligence&quot; Charm would allow. Same death penalty.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T11:14:34-08:00","id":775560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=775557#post775557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to see more Butterfly Eyes charms as a set of various tricks that work as illusion-by-tricking-you-into-believing-stupid-stuff-and-acting-accordingly-idiotic influence. Really powerful against single opponents, both in physical and social combat, but relatively easy to shatter if someone else points it out to the victim how stupid he acts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars should definitely be able to trick and fool and feint, but their sleight of hand isn't going to involve phantasmal illusions of light or sound. (Hallucinations born of inflicted madness, however...)<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But we've been told that Lunars <i>can </i>shape how others perceive them, and of course they can shape their own bodies, so...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'd like Lunars to be able to completely soak an attack but make it seem like they were badly wounded. They might actually have to take a wound penalty to their next couple of actions to &quot;sell&quot; the damage to their opponent, but they can drop the act to launch a surprise offensive.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In reverse, I'd like Lunars to be able to become badly wounded but make it seem like they soaked the damage completely. They still actually suffer wound penalties, and the greater the penalty, the easier it is for the opponent to see through the deception.<br /> <br /> And you can upgrade it still further.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The 2.5 errata introduced an Abyssal soak Charm that, as a knock-on effect, would inflict an attacker (and witnesses?) with horror if the Abyssal completely soaked the attack with the Charm. If that can be an incidental effect of a Resistance-based soak Charm, then a Lunar could use a whole Charm to upgrade his &quot;pretend I wasn't hurt&quot; social-Attribute Charm to have similar effects. Terrify your enemies or inspire your allies with your appearance of invincibility.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On the flipside, use your facade of injury to inspire your enemy to overconfidence.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Naturally, these Charms have cousins and allies in my earlier suggestions for Charm that you use to fool your enemy about whether you're using a hit-and-run strategy out of fear or whimsy.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I also want a Charm for convincing my opponents that I'm stalking and striking at them from the shadows because I'm too weak to face them directly... so that they'll underestimate my actual strength and lower their guard.<br /> <br /> Conversely, I also want to convince my hunters that I'm hitting and running because I'm so much stronger than them that I feel like having fun... even though it's really because I'd be totally screwed in a direct confrontation, and I need to discourage them from taking the initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T11:31:17-08:00","id":775564,"title":"","content":"Anyone familiar with the <i>Monster Hunter</i> franchise?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.techdollogic.com/rf.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> However Lunar crafting Charms compare to those of other Exalted, I want Lunars to have <i>superhuman facility</i> with turning the trophies of their hunts into functioning, durable weapons and armor. Trophies from slain demons, elementals, and gods should also be valid targets, especially for crafting artifact gear.<br /> <br /> <br /> To further this vein, I want a Charm that, when you wear an animal's hide, you can treat the creature as a True Form. Which is a cool compromise between the setting's particular rules on Heart's Blood and the stories of skinwalkers who actually need an animal's (or person's) skin in order to shapeshift.<br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps an upgrade would even let you assume a different war form based on that creature, to the extent that the creature resembled an animal or had an alternative, bestial form.<br /> <br /> Like, I could turn a Solar's skull into a helmet, and if he had a Lion Icon for his anima banner, I could assume a Lion war form. (And now you have a special reason to hunt down the First and Forsaken Lion.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T11:36:38-08:00","id":775566,"title":"","content":"&lt;stuff removed&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":643,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","user":"Taliesin","date":".  Not wanted in this thread. 11-27-2015, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T12:21:19-08:00","id":775579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=775566#post775566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know what the devs hinted about Lunars and their capabilities, but that doesn't stop me from wanting something different.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it would be nice if we could restrict this thread to Charm requests we can reasonably expect to have fulfilled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T12:33:48-08:00","id":775585,"title":"","content":"Do you think the very meta Butterfly Eyes Charms are at all likely to come back? Like &quot;your opponent is convinced you have leveraged a defense they cannot pierce, thus affecting their actions.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe my nostalgia for them is they had actual thematic coherence and weren't simply Silver Solar stuff. <br /> <br /> If animal imagery is necessary, to me they represent something like...how the nonpoisonous viceroy butterfly looks like the poisonous monarch and therefore things avoid eating it too. Or how some snakes have similar, but not exactly the same, banding as the red-yellow-black coral snake, and have a survival advantage through that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T14:44:47-08:00","id":775635,"title":"","content":"I want a charm that lets you trade health levels for non-charm bonuses on a Clash attempt by just taking some injury to get inside your opponent's guard, like a boar running straight up a spear to gore someone, or the finale of <i>Rob Roy</i> where Liam Neeson gets a lot of stinging flesh wounds from Tim Roth until Roth over-commits, then cuts him in half.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T15:07:45-08:00","id":775647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=775635#post775635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want a charm that lets you trade health levels for non-charm bonuses on a Clash attempt by just taking some injury to get inside your opponent's guard, like a boar running straight up a spear to gore someone, or the finale of <i>Rob Roy</i> where Liam Neeson gets a lot of stinging flesh wounds from Tim Roth until Roth over-commits, then cuts him in half.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Bruce Lee?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bruce Lee</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forget about winning and losing; forget about pride and pain.<b> Let your opponent graze your skin and you smash into his flesh; let him smash into your flesh and you fracture his bones; let him fracture your bones and you take his life!</b> Do not be concerned with escaping safely- lay your life before him!!</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: &quot;Be Moonsilver, my friend&quot; ? ^__^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T00:23:17-08:00","id":775840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=775585#post775585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think the very meta Butterfly Eyes Charms are at all likely to come back? Like &quot;your opponent is convinced you have leveraged a defense they cannot pierce, thus affecting their actions.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Exalted already modeled something like this far better with Feral Smile Tactic, and similar Solar/Abyssal Presence Charms.<br /> <br /> Your opponent thinking you're terrifyingly invincible and dangerous (as per those intimidation Charms) isn't really that much different from your opponent thinking that attacking you will have no effect.<br /> <br /> The Butterfly Eye Defense Charm ultimately just forced enemies to spend a Willpower to strike you, and that's not a bad effect. But one needs to recognize that such an effect is ultimately what the Charm does, and hammer the meta-gaming into mere flavor along the lines of &quot;I'm super-scary as hell&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Lunar needs to accept a real weakness in return for that fake strength. For example, the Lunar is working so hard to sell the idea that she cannot be harmed that she must use a Full Defense action (even though it may not seem that way to observers) and cannot attack that turn... perhaps she cannot even move, because needing to move would break the illusion that she has no need to evade or retreat.<br /> <br /> This is similar to my idea of how a Lunar needs to accept real wound penalties in order to sell the idea that she's mortally wounded, even though she's perfectly healthy... or how the Lunar needs to find a way to hide her real wound penalties from her real injuries in order to sell the idea that she's perfectly health instead of really being mortally wounded.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if the Lunar fakes the idea that her next attack is a Super Ultimate Death-Kill Murder Strike, she needs to accept some sort of vulnerability. Something that system transparency renders into a gamble for the defender -- if the defender calls the Lunar's bluff, she can hurt the Lunar really bad, but she has to accept some consequence in return.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If animal imagery is necessary, to me they represent something like...how the nonpoisonous viceroy butterfly looks like the poisonous monarch and therefore things avoid eating it too. Or how some snakes have similar, but not exactly the same, banding as the red-yellow-black coral snake, and have a survival advantage through that? </div> </div> </div>The Lunar Tell is a functional thing now, in the corebook. Functional enough that Lunars could have a disguise Charm as good as the Alchemical one. One that lets a Lunar mimic someone they haven't eaten.<br /> <br /> Going by your inspiration, a Lunar who assumes the form of someone significantly stronger than himself/the opponent can appear to be as strong as the person he's imitating... so long as someone doesn't spot his Tell, just as someone who suddenly recognizes the difference between the coral snake and king snake knows that the faker isn't so scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T10:30:31-08:00","id":776089,"title":"","content":"Going back to the ideas of &quot;turn my hunting trophies into gear&quot; and &quot;wearing gear made from an animal lets me treat it as a true form&quot; and &quot;there's a possibility that your spirit shape is merely the first animal form you get and the only one you get automatically, but it isn't mechanically superior to any other animal form, because then you're not pressured to choose a totem based on utility&quot;...<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd like a way to get my beast-weapon and beast-armor from my own Spirit Shape / Totem without having to hunt down and murder the closest mortal equivalent.<br /> <br /> Not because I'm opposed to killing, but because &quot;killing my kindred spirit&quot; never sat right with me. I am The Wolf already, so why should I kill a wolf to become The Wolf?<br /> <br /> <br /> It might be nice to instead have a Face Yourself ritual, where you fight your own Totem and symbolically overcome yourself, so that you can make your trophy-gear from yourself.<br /> <br /> This might be related to the final two options I listed in my post on &quot;familiar Charms&quot;. The possibility of splitting your human form or spirit shape off to act as a temporary familiar.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a related note, I would also like the option of using a Lunar's Spirit Shape as a war form, rather than a hybrid shape. Like, whatever benefits a Lunar gets in war form aside from opposable thumbs and being able to stand and run like a human being, I'd like to get in a purely animal form.<br /> <br /> To put it in classic <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i> terms, choosing to use Hispo (near-wolf) rather than Crinos (man-wolf).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-28-2015, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T10:32:46-08:00","id":776091,"title":"","content":"<b>Snake Head Defense</b><br /> I want a Charm that turns my immediate personal space (ie: being in the same range band as me) into an environmental hazard zone for enemies.<br /> <br /> When they get close enough, my hair becomes snakes, my tail becomes an independently moving scorpion's barb, my cloak becomes the beating, bone-breaking wings of a swan, crows fly out of my sleeves, rats boil up from my shadow... <i>Whatever</i> manifestation best fits my character, <i>that</i> pestilence befalls my foes when they approach me.<br /> <br /> A bit more creatively flexible than the old Snake Head Defense... and mechanically simpler.<br /> <br /> An upgrade would allow me to sic this plague of beasts upon distance enemies, a la <b>Thousandfold Wasp Dance</b>, at the cost of denying me the protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T10:48:21-08:00","id":776096,"title":"","content":"Going back to crafting and lair Charms, I want Lunars to have the power to create stuff that inspires pants-wetting terror or tunnel-vision desire in anyone who beholds them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Gouge my claw marks into someone's door? They decide to leave their land.<br /> <br /> Carve an effigy to serve as a border-stone? No one passes through that way.<br /> <br /> Create a den? Only the bravest of warriors will dare to enter.<br /> <br /> Scar my emissary, or dress him in war paint or sacred priestly garb of my own design? No dude is man enough to fuck with him, at least or especially when he is on my business.<br /> <br /> Piss in the woods? The smell terrifies people into avoiding my territory.<br /> <br /> You don't want to piss in the woods? Please pay attention, because I first mentioned multiple options that don't involve urination. You could just as easily put up a very fancy Keep Out sign, or leave a sock on the door handle. The concept isn't about urination, but supplementing ANY action that marks an object to warn people that it belongs to you. Pissing has the advantage of being real easy, but as the urine is washed or evaporated away, the Charm's effect dies with it. That's why a Lunar looking for a more permanent border-marker will carve marks into large rocks or stone cliff faces.<br /> <br /> <br /> In reverse, I can bait traps with pretty objects people see and must have, cook meals that draw men from miles around as the smell carries on the wind, prepare lairs that seem welcoming and homey, or simply leave a careless trail of clothes leading to the bedroom which even the most principled Dragon-Blooded officer can't resist.<br /> <br /> Or for giggles, I make a golden ring that people murder each other to own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T12:38:54-08:00","id":776145,"title":"","content":"Circe's Lament (or choose a more setting appropriate name): Animal shapes you get cursed into should count as part of your suite of shapes once you find a Lunar-appropriate mechanism of recovering from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/214-brontes","name":"Brontes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T13:39:06-08:00","id":776179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brontes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=776145#post776145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Circe's Lament (or choose a more setting appropriate name): Animal shapes you get cursed into should count as part of your suite of shapes once you find a Lunar-appropriate mechanism of recovering from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go one step further, to make this niche ability more useful and worth buying.<br /> <br /> Circe's Lament is, at BASE, a Charm that allows a Lunar to reject any imposed transformation through using Heart's Blood shapeshifting to assume any form (or at least your true form), and in so doing the Lunar gains the form that the enemy attempted to impose upon him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:05:09-08:00","id":776191,"title":"","content":"<b>Attention-Demanding Presence (Appearance)</b><br /> Without making any overt action or sound at all, a Lunar shouts with her very being to announce her presence. All characters within a particular radius become aware of the Lunar's exact location, even if their usual senses cannot perceive her. All affected characters are compelled to relocate such that they are capable of watching or listening to her, and then to silently and peacefully pay attention to her until she begins to perform, speak or otherwise communicate. The effect cannot compel characters to place themselves in danger or any particularly awkward positions, and they decide how quickly they wish to relocate. The compulsion effect is broken if the Lunar herself moves with any urgency or initiates combat.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Notes:</b> Lunars walks into a noisy city square, pops this Charm, waits for an audience, then turns the stage over to her Solar partner with his Respect-Commanding Attitude. Or she just launches into her own performance and captivates their attention in some other way.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Observed Prey Instinct (Perception)</b><br /> As long as this Charm remains active, the Lunar becomes instantly aware whenever anyone is focusing his attention upon her, though she does not automatically discern who he is, where he is, how he is observing her, or why. The Lunar <i>does </i>know exactly how many individual creatures are observing her at any given moment, and <i>which </i>of the creatures she can perceive are among those paying attention to her.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Notes:</b> Definite synergy with Attention-Demanding Presence; you make everyone in the area turn their eyes toward you, and then count up all the observers you </i>can't<i> detect. Of course, for a Lunar trying to fly under the radar, OPI can be used by itself. An upgrade would extend the effect to include non-character observers like cameras and other animate sensors she's triggering. A different upgrade would allow the Lunar the chance to discern where unnoticed observers are in relation to her, or from what vantage point someone is remotely watching her (whether by spell or video camera).</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:06:09-08:00","id":776192,"title":"","content":"<b>Hide of the Cunning Hunter<br /> --- Perfect Symmetry<br /> --- --- False Invulnerability<br /> --- --- Fake Endurance<br /> --- Shaping the Ideal Form / Changing Plumage Mastery<br /> --- Masking the Brilliant Form<br /> --- Shifting Penumbra Stance<br /> --- One of the Herd<br /> --- Subtle Chameleon Practice<br /> --- --- Inexplicable Lunar Wonders</b><br /> <b>--- One of the Herd<br /> --- --- Clover Can't Be Found<br /> --- --- Forgetful Victim Prana<br /> <br /> <br /> Hide of the Cunning Hunter (Manipulation)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Conceal distinguishing marks and cosmetic disfigurements.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Perfect Symmetry (Manipulation - follows Hide of the Cunning Hunter)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Conceal crippling disfigurements and obvious wounds. Observers get a chance to see through this disguise every time they witness you performing an action which suffers from a wound penalty or missing body part, but \u2013 as per the previewed Abyssal Charm, Incorruptible Beauty \u2013 the Exalt can suffer no Appearance penalties that are not the result of Charms or magic that directly affect her Appearance. This Charm must be invoked once per individual wound, with more grievous wounds incurring larger costs.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>False Invulnerability (Manipulation - follows Perfect Symmetry)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Inflict your attacker (and possibly any witnesses) with horror if you immediately used Perfect Symmetry to make it seem as if the attack which just struck you inflicted no damage at all.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fake Endurance (Manipulation - follows Perfect Symmetry)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You preternaturally conceal any signs of sleep deprivation, exhaustion, hunger, thirst, shortness of breath, or low mote pools.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shaping the Ideal Form / Changing Plumage Mastery </b><b>(Manipulation - follows Hide of the Cunning Hunter)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Alter cosmetic details, including gender, build, apparent age, voice, and scent.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Masking the Brilliant Form </b><b>(Manipulation - follows Hide of the Cunning Hunter)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Disguise one's Castemark and anima banner to appear as a different Lunar Caste or a member of a completely different Exalted Host.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shifting Penumbra Stance </b><b>(Manipulation - follows Hide of the Cunning Hunter)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Lunar ignites her anima to the bonfire level, warping her body and heroic spirit to remove all distinguishing traces. Insufficiently perceptive observers are completely incapable of determining the Lunar's nature or identity, for all that the Lunar cannot even attempt to hide her presence. Her voice and scent also become completely indistinct. However, this Charm does nothing to affect the memories of those who have already observed her features.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> But just because people can't distinguish any of her features any more, that doesn't mean they can't recognize her from moment to moment. If she vanishes from sight only to reappear, witnesses will recognize that she's the same creature. Every time she talks, they know it's the same creature talking. Her scent also remains a valid way to track her, even if the hounds have no idea what they're hunting. Tracking her by her footprints is possible, but they first have to correctly guess that those prints belong to her when they cannot remember the shape of her feet or the weight of her body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>One of the Herd (Manipulation - follows Hide of the Cunning Hunter)</b><br /> A more restrained trick than Shifting Penumbra Stance; so long as the Lunar's anima does <i>not </i>flare, anyone who observes her will be completely incapable of recalling any details about any voices, scents or appearances she displayed while under this Charm's effect. Even if she was the only lizard woman in a crowd of mortal men, witnesses will only remember her words and actions. The effects of this Charm come into play after the scene is over.<br /> <br /> Any witnesses will recall any of the Lunar's previous appearances, voices or scents they observed if they encounter them again in any fashion; this includes even second-hand encounters, such as another character asking if they have met anyone meeting a matching description, or seeing a wanted poster.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clover Can't be Found (Manipulation - follows One of the Herd)</b><br /> Witnesses forget the Lunar's distinguishing features <i>as soon as they take their eyes off of her</i>. This doesn't work if they can listen to the Lunar's voice at the time. Characters capable of detecting the Lunar's scent also cannot be fooled unless the Lunar manages to banish her scent from the area.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Forgetful Victim Prana (Manipulation - follows One of the Herd)</b><br /> The Lunar makes it more difficult for witnesses to be reminded of her features in any future encounters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Subtle Chameleon Practice </b><b>(Manipulation - follows Hide of the Cunning Hunter)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">By paying a mote surcharge, the Lunar may treat any disguise Charm as though it had the Mute keyword.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-29-2015, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:45:09-08:00","id":776218,"title":"","content":"Okay, Manipulation is deception, whether malevolent or benevolent or neither. And Charisma is sincerity.<br /> <br /> I'm recalling what Holden said: If Solar Charms tend to express &quot;I can&quot;, Lunar Charms tend to express &quot;I am&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thus, Lunar social influence Charms based on Charisma will be all about total honesty. The Lunar cannot use them to deceive, exaggerate, or otherwise convince anyone of anything that he doesn't believe.<br /> <br /> So in return, he can use Charisma Charms to convince people he is definitely absolutely telling the utter truth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>BEAST-CALMING METHOD</b><br /> As detailed in the original post. This Charm lives and dies based on the Lunar's sincerity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>LORE-SPEAKING METHOD</b><br /> No matter how absurd the claim, no matter how rude the delivery, no matter how unsightly the Lunar's grooming or alien his form, the Lunar speaks the truth as best he understands it, and is believed. Yes, your father the king used to be a woman beggar on the street before I helped her. Yes, the girl down the street really is worth falling in love with. Yes, despite appearances, this sword really is worth that bargain. Yes, the task I am persuading you to pursue really isn't as dangerous as you've been led to believe. Yes, despite appearances, I really can and will rip your face off if you take one more step.<br /> <br /> The force of the Lunar's earnestly declared truth is so powerful that those exposed to it more strongly resist social influences which attempt to deceive and confuse them. More than one poor village has been murdered in holocaust to destroy the heresy that the Silver Anathema are not demons.<br /> <br /> The Lunar may use this Charm on himself to better help herself defend against liars who can make coal seem white, though it doesn't help for remembering starry-eyed trouble-makers after they've gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>CHARISMATIC LUNAR TRICK</b><br /> The stronger the Lunar believes, the stronger his arguments. The Lunar adds a number of dice to his social influence roll, equal to the intensity of his most relevant Intimacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>BROTHERHOOD OF LAKE AND RIVER</b><br /> As an upgrade to Charismatic Lunar Trick, if the Lunar is reaching the target through an Intimacy of hers which matches his own, or if she is currently in the grips of the same strong mood that holds the Lunar in its sway, she increases any penalty derived from that Intimacy or mood for the purposes of refusing his influence. If the target resists the Lunar's social influence using an Intimacy opposed to the Lunar's own, reduce the bonus that the target would normally gain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>IT'S A PROMISE</b><br /> Whether swearing salvation or revenge, the strength of the Lunar's honesty binds himself to do as he says. He creates in himself a Principle for that task, with an intensity equal to the challenge, and he cannot voluntarily rid himself of that Principle until his work is completed. In the meantime, his beneficiaries derive hope and his opponents derive fear from the sure knowledge that the Lunar will not stop until he has fulfilled his word.<br /> <br /> <br /> Without bringing back the ability for Lunars to learn Fair Folk Charms, I still want Lunar Exalted to be able to swear to magically binding oaths like the one above, with various different effects. Blood oaths, if you will, since blood is an important currency for Lunars.<br /> <br /> A blood oath where you swear to protect and provide for someone as a subordinate, while they swear to obey and serve you in return. Just as with the similar bond between you and familiar, this allows your new follower to <i>gift</i> you with their Heart's Blood without you needing to hunt them. They have accepted you as alpha, what more dominance could you possibly hold over them?<br /> <br /> In reverse, an oath sworn between equals could grant you the other party's Heart's Blood if they break the oath before you do, but because you swore the oath sincerely through a Charisma Charm, you are also bound to uphold it and will suffer consequences if you break it first instead.<br /> <br /> With other Charms (Insidious Lunar Transformation), you could not only gain the target's Heart's Blood, but curse them to assume an animal form as punishment for their oathbreaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:58:01-08:00","id":776222,"title":"","content":"I fail to see how Perfect Symmetry and Shaping the Ideal Form don't fit under Appearance? That wouldn't even necessarily keep them from having a Manipulation charm as a pre-req (Solars get some cross-Ability stuff in 3e, iirc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T15:17:29-08:00","id":776234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=776222#post776222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fail to see how Perfect Symmetry and Shaping the Ideal Form don't fit under Appearance? That wouldn't even necessarily keep them from having a Manipulation charm as a pre-req (Solars get some cross-Ability stuff in 3e, iirc).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Charm I've labeled &quot;Perfect Symmetry&quot; is about manipulating other people into thinking you aren't injured.<br /> <br /> And back when I was writing these concepts, I had to answer the question of &quot;what determines whether it is Charisma, Manipulation, or Appearance&quot;?<br /> <br /> The best answer I came up with was Sincerity, Lying, and Either/Or.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's not get too literal about the word &quot;appearance&quot;, since Manipulation is the Attribute that lets you &quot;appear&quot; honest so long as no one beats your Guile. Should the Appearance Attribute and its Charms affect your Guile just because the normal word &quot;appearance&quot; has a broader use than the Appearance Attribute's name?<br /> <br /> <br /> But whether or not Shaping the Ideal Form counts as lying for a Lunar Exalt is a matter of interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T15:52:36-08:00","id":776245,"title":"","content":"Not really sure I agree with that breakdown, but fair enough, I suppose. I do prefer a more literal interpretation of &quot;Appearance,&quot; and a less binary charm division than &quot;am I lying?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T16:47:44-08:00","id":776268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=776245#post776245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really sure I agree with that breakdown, but fair enough, I suppose. I do prefer a more literal interpretation of &amp;quot;Appearance,&amp;quot; and a less binary charm division than &amp;quot;am I lying?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'd choose to have three different social Attributes, where one is more of a Merit and the other two can be hard to distinguish from each other except that one can be used to command others and the other can be used to deceive others, but I have to work with what I've got.<br /> <br /> Convincing Sincerity and Convincing Lies are the best I can do, and Appearance applies equally to either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:02:09-08:00","id":776321,"title":"","content":"Lunars should not have anything comparable to Wyld Shaping Technique. But I feel there's a middle-ground between Wyld-Shaping Technique and Ritual of Lunar Stability that hasn't been sufficiently explored.<br /> <br /> Lunars can't create permanent, ordered lands out of the Wyld? Fine. But could Lunars at least have the power to reshape the local Wyld into a particular brand of wonderland more favorable to them than to their enemies?<br /> <br /> Preferably with the ability to use Ritual of Lunar Stability not only to protect Creation from the Wyld, but to prevent raksha from trying to change altered stretches of Wyld into something unfavorable to the Lunar.<br /> <br /> <br /> Creation's history is being rewritten such that the Lunars actually fit within it, and so they do not need to be swept under the Wyld rug until the setting is ready for them to sudden start existing. Previously, Lunar history was written so that the Wyld pretty much stomped all over them, and Lunar Charms had to be written such that this made sense. Previously, Chimerism was made worse and more important than the Lunar Great Curse.<br /> <br /> That's not the case anymore. Now the Wyld Hunt and Sidereals are the chief historical dangers to the Lunar Exalted. Now the Lunars broke their own Castes themselves as a deliberate action to reinvent themselves for their new circumstances. Now Chimerism is similarly deliberate, and the Great Curse is the proper source of horror. Now the Lunars can be allowed to resist the Wyld more completely than before.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm certainly not asking for the return of the Wyld keyword, but the Solar Exalted never needed that keyword to have good reasons for seeking out the Wyld, nor to have the power to make it their bitch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T17:07:00-08:00","id":776889,"title":"","content":"I'd like something along the line's of Ban's ability Physical Hunt, from the manga/anime <i>Seven Deadly Sins.</i> For those unfamiliar, he is able to temporarily steal an enemy's strength or speed, and use it to boost himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T17:11:27-08:00","id":776893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=776889#post776889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like something along the line's of Ban's ability Physical Hunt, from the manga/anime <i>Seven Deadly Sins.</i> For those unfamiliar, he is able to temporarily steal an enemy's strength or speed, and use it to boost himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Through what method or medium does he steal their power?<br /> <br /> Solar Lore contains a lot of tricks for moving motes, Willpower, and health around between characters, Solar Integrity has a Charm for beating up a god to copy some of its Charms, and Solar Occult can DIGEST spirits, so it's not impossible for some kind of Intelligence Charm to do what you ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T20:41:05-08:00","id":776972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see#post775260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sleeping Dragon Awakens</b> was a very flavorful and powerful Charm from 2.5 that didn't get long to shine. But I have recently realized that the character of the Charm can be preserved by replacing the Overdrive mechanic with bonuses to your Join Battle roll. Rather than building up a stock of Offensive motes to blow away invaders to your territory, you can build up a stock of Initiative to seize the first strike and possibly end the battle with a single Decisive blow. Or at least take out one of the invaders before engaging the others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Who Disturbs My Slumber</b>, created by Reminiscent Oasis, can do the same. Instead of gaining offensive motes upon being rudely awoken from your sleep, you gain automatic successes to your Join Battle roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast Calming Method</b> would be a Charisma-based Charm that functions like Solar Friendship With Animals Approach, but without that Charm's Survival Ability limitations. With the Charm active, the Lunar doesn't register as a threat to anyone or anything -- wounded beasts, small prey animals, and mother hippos watching their young will allow him to approach and touch them, and territorial predators will allow him to pass through their hunting grounds unmolested so long as they are not hungry. The Lunar could even break into someone's home in full armor and bearing a bloody sword, and the homeowner will react with indignation regarding the trespass instead of fear for her life. Even the most convicted Immaculate, if she learned he was a Lunar Anathema, would believe that the silver demon meant her no harm. Those so affected will not mistake a lack of harmful intent for a lack of danger, however; Immaculate devotees will remember that devils are inherently corruptive, just as beasts that smell an infectious disease upon the Lunar would seek to flee or drive him away, and mice will take care that they are not trodden underfoot by accident.<br /> <br /> The effects of this Charm end immediately upon the Lunar deciding to engage in hostilities with any other present character, or otherwise take an action that would indirectly harm them. Studying someone with premeditated intent to harm them later with the information counts, though plotting murder against someone not present would not. The Charm cannot be reactivated for the rest of the scene, and will not work again on witnesses to the Lunar's hostility until the next day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dog-Tongue Method.</b> Speak any human language (or your own true voice!), so long as your current form is capable of vocalizing at all. Likewise, communicate with any animal species regardless of your form, so long as they communicate in a manner even vaguely possible with your form -- wearing the form of a wolf would be ineffective for conveying ideas to a species of octopus that exchange information primarily through changing color patterns. This Charm doesn't itself grant the Lunar knowledge of an animal species's language, nor incline animals to listen.<br /> <br /> <b>Stance-as-Thought Stride.</b> As the Solar Charm, Poetic Expression Style, but it additionally allows the Lunar to communicate simple ideas to animal species even without knowing their language. Having the appropriate Survival specialty allows the communication of complex ideas beyond what the animal's own language ought to convey, though the animal's own intelligence still limits the complexity of what they can understand.<br /> <br /> <b>Glance Oration Technique.</b> As Single-Voice Kata, but through body-language. The Lunar can speak, sing, or play an instrument in order to attract the attention of those who can hear but not immediately see him, but this Charm doesn't enable him to convey two different messages at once. Unlike Single Voice Kata, spirits and fair folk actually like this method of communication, but the Lunar's Appearance becomes capped by his Performance since these exotic beings are judging the delivery of his arguments based on the beauty of his interpretative dancing.<br /> <br /> <b>Secret Speech Method.</b> A Manipulation Charm that allows the Lunar to communicate one message to an individual or small group, and an entirely different message to everyone else. Explicitly compatible with Glance Oration Technique, allowing the Lunar to hide the message of his body language from the broader audience, or from a particular individual or subgroup.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to see:<br /> -FLESH-SCULPTING ART<br /> -LUNAR BLOOD SHAPING TECHNIQUE<br /> -INSIDIOUS LUNAR TRANSFORMATION<br /> -FORM-DESTROYING TOUCH<br /> -CLAY-WETTING PRACTICE<br /> -SCORPION AND TOAD MASTERY<br /> -MOON AND EARTH BLESSING<br /> -LIMB-SHIELDING GROWTH<br /> -SILVER COIN BARGAIN<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T22:39:00-08:00","id":777009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=776972#post776972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd like to see:<br /> -FLESH-SCULPTING ART<br /> -LUNAR BLOOD SHAPING TECHNIQUE<br /> -INSIDIOUS LUNAR TRANSFORMATION<br /> -FORM-DESTROYING TOUCH<br /> -CLAY-WETTING PRACTICE<br /> -SCORPION AND TOAD MASTERY<br /> -MOON AND EARTH BLESSING<br /> -LIMB-SHIELDING GROWTH<br /> -SILVER COIN BARGAIN</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Blood Reshaping Technique definite ought to return, and Insidious Lunar Transformation. Flesh-Sculpting Art and Clay-Wetting Practice might become names for how Lunars use feeding their blood to people as a way to make it easier to heal and/or mutate them.<br /> <br /> Limb-Shielding Growth seems to fall into the Liminal field these days, if not the Abyssal field. Making a shield of bone burst from your forearm doesn't seem very &quot;werewolf demigod&quot;. Hatewheel is on record as removing the limb-stretching stuff from Lunars for similar reasons, whereas I could see that kind of grotesquerie fitting the corpse-Exalted who tear themselves apart in horrific transformations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T23:12:03-08:00","id":777024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=777009#post777009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunar Blood Reshaping Technique definite ought to return, and Insidious Lunar Transformation. Flesh-Sculpting Art and Clay-Wetting Practice might become names for how Lunars use feeding their blood to people as a way to make it easier to heal and/or mutate them.<br /> <br /> Limb-Shielding Growth seems to fall into the Liminal field these days, if not the Abyssal field. Making a shield of bone burst from your forearm doesn't seem very &quot;werewolf demigod&quot;. Hatewheel is on record as removing the limb-stretching stuff from Lunars for similar reasons, whereas I could see that kind of grotesquerie fitting the corpse-Exalted who tear themselves apart in horrific transformations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding LSG:<br /> <br /> 1 - it probably wouldn't be a shield-looking affixation of naked, pale bone, but something that has a horn sheathing on it and more closely resembles, well, something grown.<br /> <br /> 2 - It probably doesn't burst out of the limb. I've never envisioned it working that way, personally; it originally built on an effect that grows armored flesh over the Lunar's body, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T01:30:05-08:00","id":777051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=776889#post776889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like something along the line's of Ban's ability Physical Hunt, from the manga/anime <i>Seven Deadly Sins.</i> For those unfamiliar, he is able to temporarily steal an enemy's strength or speed, and use it to boost himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually more like Sidereal Larceny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T02:23:44-08:00","id":777063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=775560#post775560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars should definitely be able to trick and fool and feint, but their sleight of hand isn't going to involve phantasmal illusions of light or sound. (Hallucinations born of inflicted madness, however...)<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But we've been told that Lunars <i>can </i>shape how others perceive them, and of course they can shape their own bodies, so...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'd like Lunars to be able to completely soak an attack but make it seem like they were badly wounded. They might actually have to take a wound penalty to their next couple of actions to &quot;sell&quot; the damage to their opponent, but they can drop the act to launch a surprise offensive.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In reverse, I'd like Lunars to be able to become badly wounded but make it seem like they soaked the damage completely. They still actually suffer wound penalties, and the greater the penalty, the easier it is for the opponent to see through the deception.<br /> <br /> And you can upgrade it still further.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect soak AND make it look like you're badly hurt sound a bit to much for one charm. I'ld say split it into two charms. But yeah saound good.<br /> <br /> I would also suggest if you like those kind of tricks : charms that trick the opponents into thinking you're crashed when you're not (and/or the opposite)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=775560#post775560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The 2.5 errata introduced an Abyssal soak Charm that, as a knock-on effect, would inflict an attacker (and witnesses?) with horror if the Abyssal completely soaked the attack with the Charm. If that can be an incidental effect of a Resistance-based soak Charm, then a Lunar could use a whole Charm to upgrade his &quot;pretend I wasn't hurt&quot; social-Attribute Charm to have similar effects. Terrify your enemies or inspire your allies with your appearance of invincibility.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On the flipside, use your facade of injury to inspire your enemy to overconfidence.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Naturally, these Charms have cousins and allies in my earlier suggestions for Charm that you use to fool your enemy about whether you're using a hit-and-run strategy out of fear or whimsy.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I also want a Charm for convincing my opponents that I'm stalking and striking at them from the shadows because I'm too weak to face them directly... so that they'll underestimate my actual strength and lower their guard.<br /> <br /> Conversely, I also want to convince my hunters that I'm hitting and running because I'm so much stronger than them that I feel like having fun... even though it's really because I'd be totally screwed in a direct confrontation, and I need to discourage them from taking the initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm always a bit cautious about tricks about &quot;strategies&quot;, and fight styles. They seem too convoluted and possibly railroad the enemy into stupid choices (ok) but for dubious reasons, or limited &quot;counterplay&quot; (not ok) and if you &quot;nerf&quot; them they become too situational and weak. Just like I said for the arms of the unconquered sun style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T02:28:33-08:00","id":777064,"title":"","content":"Considering that initiative itself is an abstraction for folks trying to kill each other, a Charm to &quot;fake&quot; being in Crash seems a little too much like shenanigans. Plus, you gain bonus Initiative when you Crash someone, yeah? Shouldn't the guy who &quot;Crashes&quot; the Lunar know better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T02:42:04-08:00","id":777072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=777064#post777064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that initiative itself is an abstraction for folks trying to kill each other, a Charm to &quot;fake&quot; being in Crash seems a little too much like shenanigans. Plus, you gain bonus Initiative when you Crash someone, yeah? Shouldn't the guy who &quot;Crashes&quot; the Lunar know better?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. Yes initiative, as a number, is an abstraction but being &quot;crashed&quot; is a binary state that means something. Not always exactly the same thing but still.<br /> It can be losing your balance, stumble on an object, failing a heavy sword swing possibly having it stuck in the environment (a tree?) and leaving yourself open for attack.<br /> <br /> As for the initiative bonus, coudn't it be part of the &quot;trick&quot; to make the enemy believe he has the advantage? As you said initiative is an abstraction, and I don't expect the enemy to have such an accurate knowledge of the exact number that you can't mess with his perception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T02:52:44-08:00","id":777077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=777072#post777072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the initiative bonus, coudn't it be part of the &quot;trick&quot; to make the enemy believe he has the advantage? As you said initiative is an abstraction, and I don't expect the enemy to have such an accurate knowledge of the exact number that you can't mess with his perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way you could do that is to tie it to your Guile. Have it cost 5 initiative - (Guile) that goes to your opponent. Thus the better you are at hiding your motives already the less you have to do to make it convincing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T06:52:07-08:00","id":777121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=777009#post777009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunar Blood Reshaping Technique definite ought to return, and Insidious Lunar Transformation. Flesh-Sculpting Art and Clay-Wetting Practice might become names for how Lunars use feeding their blood to people as a way to make it easier to heal and/or mutate them.<br /> <br /> Limb-Shielding Growth seems to fall into the Liminal field these days, if not the Abyssal field. Making a shield of bone burst from your forearm doesn't seem very &quot;werewolf demigod&quot;. Hatewheel is on record as removing the limb-stretching stuff from Lunars for similar reasons, whereas I could see that kind of grotesquerie fitting the corpse-Exalted who tear themselves apart in horrific transformations.</div> </div> </div> </div>LSG could easily be refluffed as growing a shell, or additional limbs or something in that vein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T07:36:02-08:00","id":777141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=777063#post777063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect soak AND make it look like you're badly hurt sound a bit to much for one charm. I'ld say split it into two charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was never meant to be one Charm. What I meant is that even IF the Lunar manages to completely soak an attack, he could fake having suffered the full damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would also suggest if you like those kind of tricks : charms that trick the opponents into thinking you're crashed when you're not (and/or the opposite) </div> </div> </div>Black Claw Style works perfectly well with Charms fluffed around the stylist appearing weaker and more vulnerable than she really is, in a way that doesn't fool players and yet still has powerful effects on characters.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about overly meta Charms like Butterfly Eyes Defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T13:25:22-08:00","id":777328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=776893#post776893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Through what method or medium does he steal their power?<br /> <br /> Solar Lore contains a lot of tricks for moving motes, Willpower, and health around between characters, Solar Integrity has a Charm for beating up a god to copy some of its Charms, and Solar Occult can DIGEST spirits, so it's not impossible for some kind of Intelligence Charm to do what you ask.</div> </div> </div> </div>He makes a grasping motion at the person who he intends to drain. Then their blows become weaker as his grow stronger, they move more slowly as he speeds up, and so on. The longer the battle goes, the more he drains. The drain only lasts a certain amount of time, after which Ban is unable to move under his own power, as a sort of recoil as the stolen physical attributes leave him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T01:43:42-08:00","id":777625,"title":"","content":"I wonder how much room there might be for Lunars to acquire the forms of others (whether temporarily or not) through cleverly worded verbal agreements and more varied social deals. No example actually comes to mind, but it feels fitting to the mythological shapeshifter or trickster tropes that Luna's Chosen might draw from and overlap with some of their themes.<br /> <br /> The Lunar proposes to do something another isn't able or willing to in their stead. The other party agrees, and through this pact the Lunar steals their form to fulfill his part as closely as possible.<br /> <br /> The trickster happens upon a weary noble, and offers to replace them for a time, so they may rest free of burdens. The noble agrees in jest, but the trickster takes their appearance and role in truth, and is free to use it for however long their contract agreed on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 12-01-2015, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T22:07:34-08:00","id":778115,"title":"","content":"Post #29 -- I talk about my own ideas for gaining Heart's Blood through swearing and fulfilling oaths.<br /> <br /> <br /> Morke once mentioned that he wasn't a fan of temporary shape-taking; either it should be yours, or not.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know the Changing Moon in the core has such a power, but we've also been told that the Lunars' exact powers shouldn't be taken as gospel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-02-2015, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T22:10:00-08:00","id":778116,"title":"","content":"I won't bump my thread on Lunar Crafting Charm concepts, but I will link to it: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/736824-ex3-lunar-crafting-charm-concepts\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...charm-concepts</a><br /> <br /> Anteros, post #3 contains my stance on why I don't think 2ndEd's version of Clay Wetting Practice will return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:11:43-08:00","id":779157,"title":"","content":"What I would like to see are some charms that are inspired by how moon itself changes.It's the only celestial object in Creation whose &quot;face&quot; changes every night, if in a cyclical pattern over a longer stretch of time. The stars stay in their cosmic arrangements and the Sun always looks the same whenever it rises. <br /> <br /> Maybe a charm that has inflicts a mutation/pox/corruption/blight/whatever that changes over time, constantly aggravating the target who <i>just</i> got use to its previous form. Or the curse of lycanthropy, (the curse of it is losing control of your body during the transformation, only able to control it by avoiding triggers).<br /> <br /> Another could be that, after inflicting damage with a natural lethal attack, that wound will return or reopen every month under the same phase of the moon or similar rhythm. The wound that never truly heals fully and a visceral reminder to the subject and those who see it of the vindictive suffering the Chosen of Moon can induce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T13:58:22-08:00","id":779243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=779157#post779157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I would like to see are some charms that are inspired by how moon itself changes.It's the only celestial object in Creation whose &quot;face&quot; changes every night, if in a cyclical pattern over a longer stretch of time. The stars stay in their cosmic arrangements and the Sun always looks the same whenever it rises.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the stars are supposed to change far more frequently than the moon does. The Colleges aren't guaranteed to all show at the same time, in spite of the system presented in CoTD: South for Varang.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe a charm that has inflicts a mutation/pox/corruption/blight/whatever that changes over time, constantly aggravating the target who <i>just</i> got use to its previous form. Or the curse of lycanthropy, (the curse of it is losing control of your body during the transformation, only able to control it by avoiding triggers).<br /> <br /> Another could be that, after inflicting damage with a natural lethal attack, that wound will return or reopen every month under the same phase of the moon or similar rhythm. The wound that never truly heals fully and a visceral reminder to the subject and those who see it of the vindictive suffering the Chosen of Moon can induce. </div> </div> </div>Anything over time is going to need to be sparse compared to other Charms in the same field that do something immediately, because in the past, Lunars have had far too many higher level effects be slow-burning. Or dependent on the Wyld, but the latter flat out won't be a part of the Charm set, so no worries there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T09:37:43-08:00","id":784223,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to think that the <b>Beast Power Concentration</b> Charm (using all non-mutation benefits of DBT in your human form) isn't such a bad idea, after all. Especially with the new balance point that Lunars can't use Evocations in their war form.<br /> <br /> BPC becomes even more palatable if it is mirrored by <b>Titan Menagerie Method</b>, re-envisioned as a Charm that lets you apply your war form's benefits to any of your animal forms. (The spirit shape is not given special treatment, so that players are not incentivized to choose Totems based on mechanical advantages.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T22:20:36-08:00","id":785769,"title":"","content":"Other than a an Appearance that lets you, for a Limited duration, obtain or shed the Hideous merit, I'm drawing a blank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T12:49:30-08:00","id":791750,"title":"","content":"<b>Terrible Wolverine Onslaught.</b><br /> <br /> I really liked the essence of this Second Edition Charm.<br /> <br /> Granted, it was forced to be the capstone of a really crappy and confused Martial Arts Style, but the basic concept of &quot;you're pushing your body so hard for more power that it breaks down from the strain&quot; was cool. Even using the self-healing Charms to cover the damage still played into the concept, because Terrible Wolverine Onslaught meant that the Gift effects of Charms couldn't heal the wounds you were suffering from OTHER sources; so it still felt like you were pushing your body hard.<br /> <br /> Basically, it was <i>Naruto</i>'s Rock Lee using the Eight Gates.<br /> <br /> I loved the tactical dilemma of asking yourself, at the beginning of your every turn, whether the power-boost was worth the escalating risk.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind TWO being fused together with Relentless Lunar Fury, since &quot;unleashing your physical safety-limiters&quot; is generally what happens as a matter of course when you emotionally-focus your entire being upon inflicting violence. Though I'd like such a combination to also work for the retreating side of &quot;fight or flight&quot; and feats of strength like keeping a collapsing ceiling from crushing you and your friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}